    <peripheral>
      <name>WIFI_MAC_TX_QUEUE_CONTROL</name>
      <description>Four ascending physical banks represent logical EDCA queues 3,2,1,0.</description>
      <baseAddress>0x20104D34</baseAddress>
      <registers>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x10</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>PROTECTION%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Canonical WDEVTXQ_CONF2. Complete dbg_read_txq_conf2 names the three ten-bit lanes TXQ_MIN_MPDU_LEN for CBW20, CBW40 and CBW80, followed by SW_CTS at bit 30 and SW_RTS at bit 31. For HT, complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_htsig copies peer state offset 0x82 into all three lanes; complete rcUpdateAMPDUParam derives that value from the HT A-MPDU minimum MPDU start-spacing code. For HE, complete libpp[pp_he.o]::ppCalDeliNum stores the rate/GI/DCM/density-specific minimum subframe byte count at descriptor offset 0x28 and complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_hesig copies that halfword into all three lanes. The HE init suffix clears only SW_CTS in this same word, preserving SW_RTS and all three spacing lanes. A coherent hardware-owned vendor HT queue contained 0x0280a028, exactly three copies of negotiated value 40. Open HE20 MCS9 HIL with 16-us density proved value 230: fixed snapshot 0x31 lost all 32 MPDUs, while three copies of 230 received a full first-attempt BlockAck with 43 empty delimiters per non-final subframe. The descriptor-count RMWs target the separate queue-vector word at 0x20105504-q*0x7c.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>MINIMUM_MPDU_LENGTH_CBW20</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. First copy of the HT peer-derived or HE rate/density-derived minimum MPDU/subframe value.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>10</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>1023</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>MINIMUM_MPDU_LENGTH_CBW40</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Second copy of the HT peer-derived or HE rate/density-derived minimum MPDU/subframe value.</description>
              <bitOffset>10</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>10</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>1023</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>MINIMUM_MPDU_LENGTH_CBW80</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Third copy of the HT peer-derived or HE rate/density-derived minimum MPDU/subframe value.</description>
              <bitOffset>20</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>10</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>1023</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SOFTWARE_RTS</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Complete dbg_read_txq_conf2 passes bit 31 as the SW_RTS format argument at sp+4; hal_he_set_tx_protection updates this bit from its enable argument. Bounded HT40 MCS7 SGI diagnostics observe hardware-generated RTS to the data receiver followed by CTS, data and ACK/BlockAck, including control frames on both 20-MHz halves. Ordinary protected admission and the complete automatic NAV algorithm remain separate contracts.</description>
              <bitOffset>31</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SOFTWARE_CTS</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Complete dbg_read_txq_conf2 passes bit 30 as the SW_CTS format argument at sp+8. Bounded HT40 MCS7 SGI diagnostics observe hardware-generated CTS addressed to the transmitter before unicast data, on both 20-MHz halves. This establishes the request in that profile; it does not qualify the full ordinary protected-publication lifecycle.</description>
              <bitOffset>30</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x10</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>CONFIG%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Timeout, contention window, interface, AIFSN and scheduler-priority fields configured as distinct recovered RMW edges. Scheduler priority is not the original packet PTI retained in the vector bank.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x8</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>TIMEOUT</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>12</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>4095</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>CONTENTION_WINDOW</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>12</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>10</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>1023</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>INTERFACE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>22</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>3</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>AIFSN</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>24</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>15</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SCHEDULER_PRIORITY</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Complete libpp[hal_mac.o]::mac_tx_set_pti writes the unsigned minimum of packet PTI and coexistence event-one PTI here. This scheduler value is independent of the four original packet-PTI lanes in the vector bank; for Authentication and Association both values resolve to one. Open HIL read scheduler one in five reset-to-connect repetitions.</description>
              <bitOffset>28</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>15</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x10</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>CONTROL%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Descriptor address and PLCP0 format image in low 30 bits; VALID bit 30 and ENABLE bit 31 publish hardware ownership.</description>
          <addressOffset>0xC</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>DESCRIPTOR_ADDRESS_LOW</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Low twenty bits of the owned TX descriptor address; the DMA window supplies the high address bits.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>20</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>1048575</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_20_21_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Recovered PLCP0 control image; libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_plcp0 initializes these two bits to binary 10 for the ordinary direct legacy path.</description>
              <bitOffset>20</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>3</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BIT_22_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Complete pp.o ppTxFragmentProc reaches its common legacy setup at offsets 0x8e..0xa8 from the CCMP selector-three branch at 0x22a and sets descriptor bit seven. Complete hal_mac_tx.o libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_txop_q offsets 0x86..0xaa then sets this queue-control bit exactly when descriptor flag bits 7:6 equal binary 10 and clears it otherwise. Thus the bounded ordinary individual/group CCMP path sets this bit after libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_plcp0. A 2026-07-29 open HIL A/B clearing the bit increased raw ACK timeouts from the prior roughly 28 percent to 1395/2325 attempts (60 percent), so the exact set mapping is retained while the electrical meaning remains unknown.</description>
              <bitOffset>22</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BIT_23_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Recovered PLCP0 control image; libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_plcp0 initializes this bit to zero for the ordinary direct legacy path.</description>
              <bitOffset>23</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PLCP_FORMAT</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Three-bit format selector derived by complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_plcp0 from vendor descriptor flags. For the bounded plain legacy roots, libpp[pp.o]::ppTxProtoProc maps the address-one I/G bit to descriptor flag 0x2: group traffic retains format zero, while an ordinary individual-address descriptor with zero flags selects format one. Exact vendor callback images select format one for both non-A-MPDU HT20 MCS0 and HE20 MCS0 DCM S-MPDU frames; the owned open paths receive ACK at the same format. Independently captured HT and HE A-MPDU images select aggregate format two or five respectively. Format three has an instruction-exact descriptor branch but its higher-level meaning remains open. A legacy-only single-variable A/B temporarily correlated format one with status five and format zero with one authentication response, but format-zero repetitions failed; that experiment is retained as evidence that completion status alone is not a protocol-success oracle, not as an override of the complete blob mapping.</description>
              <bitOffset>24</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>3</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>7</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_27_29_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Remaining low control bits before ownership publication.</description>
              <bitOffset>27</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>3</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>7</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>VALID</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>30</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ENABLE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>31</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
      </registers>
    </peripheral>
    <peripheral>
      <name>WIFI_MAC_TX_QUEUE_VECTOR</name>
      <description>Four 0x7c-byte physical vector banks represent logical EDCA queues 3,2,1,0. The write-side Trigger-based path additionally publishes the tail of its linked MPDU-length list in the word between HE-SIG-A2 and POWER.</description>
      <baseAddress>0x20105364</baseAddress>
      <registers>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x7C</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>PLCP1%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Per-queue second PLCP/vector word. Complete dbg_read_key_entry independently names bits 22:17 as KEY_ENTRY_INDEX and bits 24:23 as BSSID_SELECT. Complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_plcp1 sets bit 29 for the guarded HT branch when descriptor word1 bit 15 selects 40-MHz channel width; the same selector is copied into HT-SIG1 CBW. A synchronous vendor raw HE20 MCS0 DCM capture used descriptor rate 0x1a and published 0x0401a000, proving that explicit DCM retains the ordinary 0x1a+MCS HE descriptor-code domain.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>LEGACY_SIGNAL</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Twelve-bit legacy PLCP SIGNAL/length value. Non-legacy formatters leave this field zero.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>12</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>4095</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RATE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Five-bit MAC rate selector published by complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_plcp1.</description>
              <bitOffset>12</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>5</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>31</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>KEY_ENTRY_INDEX</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>17</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>6</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>63</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BSSID_SELECT</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>23</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>3</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>VECTOR_FORMAT</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Three-bit vector family: zero for legacy, one for HT and two for HE in the reviewed paths.</description>
              <bitOffset>25</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>3</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>7</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>HIGH_CONTROL_28</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>28</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>CBW40</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_plcp1 sets this bit for the guarded non-HE HT40 branch.</description>
              <bitOffset>29</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>HIGH_CONTROL_31_30</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>30</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>3</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x7C</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>HE_RTS_CONTROL%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Complete hal_he_set_tx_protection optionally replaces this word with a sixteen-bit HE byte threshold and bit 16 set, clearing the disabled flag and all upper state. With no threshold publication request it leaves this word untouched. HE Operation peer programming independently sets bit 17 in all four physical queue vectors when the encoded RTS threshold is disabled.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x4</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>RTS_THRESHOLD_BYTES</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Low sixteen bits of hal_he_set_tx_protection argument a4. Complete libpp[pp_he.o]::ppCalTxHEAMPDULength stores the libpp[if_hwctrl.o]::ic_get_he_rts_threshold_bytes result at descriptor offset 0x34; libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_plcp0 loads the same word into a4. This is a PHY-specific length threshold in bytes, not a frame Duration/NAV value.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>16</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>65535</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RTS_THRESHOLD_VALID</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Set by the complete whole-word byte-threshold publication when argument a3 is nonzero.</description>
              <bitOffset>16</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>HE_RTS_DISABLED</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>17</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x7C</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>PTI%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Complete libpp[hal_mac.o]::mac_tx_set_pti publishes the original packet PTI independently into four lanes, then loads descriptor byte offset 0x22 once and passes it as argument six to hal_set_tx_pti, which publishes it as COUNT bits 31:20. This count is independent of the A-MPDU descriptor count written by libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_mplen to HT_DESCRIPTOR_COUNTS. For vendor Authentication and Association, libnet80211[ieee80211_output.o]::ieee80211_set_tx_pti event six maps through coex_pti_tab to packet PTI one; the independent scheduler field also resolves to one through the unsigned-minimum clamp against event-one PTI five. Vendor and open HIL both used 0x00111110, including the hardware-qualified 32-MPDU open profile.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x8</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>TXOP</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::hal_mac_tx_set_ppdu sets or clears this bit from descriptor word-zero bit 29 before libpp[hal_mac.o]::mac_tx_set_pti publishes the four coexistence lanes. The bit is independent of those lanes and must not retain the preceding queue transaction's value.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_1_3_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established.</description>
              <bitOffset>1</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>3</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PTI_0</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>4</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>15</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PTI_1</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>8</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>15</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PTI_2</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>12</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>15</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PTI_3</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>16</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>15</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>COUNT</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Descriptor metadata byte 0x22 passed to hal_set_tx_pti; not the A-MPDU MPDU/descriptor count.</description>
              <bitOffset>20</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>12</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>4095</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x7C</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>HE_CONTROL%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Per-queue four-byte HT-Control/HE-Control image at 0x201054e4-logical_queue*0x7c. Complete hal_he_get_htc reads the whole word. Complete libpp[hal_mac_ctl.o]::hal_he_set_htc writes the supplied word before independently selecting whether this software image overrides the hardware-generated HE-Control value.</description>
          <addressOffset>0xC</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>VALUE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Complete four-byte HE-Control image. Its A-Control subfields depend on the control ID; keep the finite protocol interpretation in the handwritten IEEE 802.11 layer rather than exposing overlapping mode-dependent SVD fields.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>32</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>4294967295</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x7C</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>HT_SIGNAL%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_htsig (size 0x23c) writes the packed HT-SIG1/HT-SIG2 queue image here for non-HE rates 16..35. Complete dbg_read_tx_sig independently prints the low MCS nibble and sixteen-bit length. The formatter copies descriptor word1 bit 15 to HT-SIG1 bit 7, whose standard meaning is CBW: zero selects 20 MHz and one selects 40 MHz. The exact vendor single-MPDU HT20 MCS0 callback image carried HT_SIGNAL=0x07006e00 for length 0x6e, confirming MCS zero, CBW20 and aggregate bit zero. Open HIL qualified the same single formatter at HT20 MCS0 LGI and HT40 MCS7 SGI. The independent two-MPDU HT20 MCS7/SGI capture carried 0x8f0c2e07 for aggregate length 0x0c2e, confirming aggregate bit one. The open direct-DMA A-MPDU path then received complete BlockAck for four separate HT40 MCS7/SGI two-MPDU submissions.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x10</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>MCS</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Seven-bit standard HT-SIG1 MCS selector. The reviewed open 1T1R path uses MCS0 through MCS7.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>7</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>127</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>CBW40</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Standard HT-SIG1 channel-width bit: zero selects 20 MHz and one selects 40 MHz.</description>
              <bitOffset>7</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>LENGTH</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Sixteen-bit HT length printed by complete dbg_read_tx_sig.</description>
              <bitOffset>8</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>16</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>65535</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SMOOTHING</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Standard HT-SIG2 smoothing bit; the reviewed formatter publishes one.</description>
              <bitOffset>24</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>NOT_SOUNDING</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Standard HT-SIG2 not-sounding bit; the reviewed formatter publishes one.</description>
              <bitOffset>25</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>REQUIRED_ONE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Required one bit retained by every reviewed HT queue vector.</description>
              <bitOffset>26</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>AGGREGATION</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Standard HT-SIG2 aggregation bit: clear for a direct MPDU and set for A-MPDU.</description>
              <bitOffset>27</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>STBC</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>28</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>3</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>FEC_CODING</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>30</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SHORT_GI</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Standard HT-SIG2 short guard-interval bit.</description>
              <bitOffset>31</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x7C</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>VHT_SIGNAL_1%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Complete dbg_read_tx_sig decodes this word only when PLCP_FORMAT is three and names VHT MCS, channel width, group ID, NSTS, SU partial AID, SGI, SGI symbol disambiguation and coding. This maps an internal hardware vector; it does not assert that the ESP32-S31 public Wi-Fi mode supports VHT transmission.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x14</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>CHANNEL_WIDTH</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_2_3_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established.</description>
              <bitOffset>2</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>GROUP_ID</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>4</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>6</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>NSTS</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>10</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>3</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SU_PARTIAL_AID</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>13</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>9</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_22_23_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established.</description>
              <bitOffset>22</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SHORT_GI</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>24</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SHORT_GI_SYMBOL_DISAMBIGUATION</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>25</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>CODING</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>26</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BIT_27_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established.</description>
              <bitOffset>27</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>MCS</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>28</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x7C</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>VHT_MODE%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Complete dbg_read_tx_sig decodes this word only when PLCP_FORMAT is three and names bits 18:2 SU_CBW20_PRE_EOFPAD_UNIT4BYTES_LEN. Remaining bits are not assigned a meaning by the complete body.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x18</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_0_1_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SU_CBW20_PRE_EOFPAD_UNIT4BYTES_LENGTH</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>2</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>17</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_19_31_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established.</description>
              <bitOffset>19</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>13</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x7C</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>HE_SU_SIGNAL_A1%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_hesig writes this HE SU vector word at 0x201054f4-q*0x7c. Live vendor MCS9 uplink images 0xfc205b4f and 0xfc605b4f independently qualify MCS nine, BSS color 27, HE20 and GI/LTF selectors one and three. A separate explicit MCS0 DCM vendor frame published 0xfc204087. Replaying the selector-one MCS9 image through the owned open DMA path received a complete 32-MPDU BlockAck on the first attempt and remained stable for more than 13,800 aggregates. Bits 31:26 are a TX-vector-required all-ones image and are not presented as on-air HE-SIG-A1 payload bits.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x1C</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>FORMAT</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BEAM_CHANGE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>1</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>UPLINK</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>2</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>MCS</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>3</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>15</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>DCM</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_hesig copies descriptor-state word at offset 0x30 bit 15 into HE-SIG-A1 bit 7. Complete libpp[trc.o]::rcGetDCMMaxRate bounds the ordinary BCC DCM rate family to MCS0, MCS1 and MCS3 according to the peer DCM receive constellation. The vendor raw-TX configuration path independently set descriptor byte +0x31 bit 7 while retaining descriptor rate 0x1a, and the live formatter published HE-SIG-A1 0xfc204087. The owned open S-MPDU path reproduced that word and received an ordinary ACK with completion status zero. Rate-bounded open A-MPDUs with 30, 29 and 26 MPDUs then received BlockAck at MCS0 for the three qualified GI/LTF selectors. Explicit DCM and rate-control fallback therefore use distinct descriptor-code domains; BPSK DCM TX is hardware-qualified for both S-MPDU and multi-subframe A-MPDU, while QPSK and 16-QAM still require a capable peer.</description>
              <bitOffset>7</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BSS_COLOR</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>8</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>6</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>63</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>VECTOR_REQUIRED_14</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_hesig ORs 0x40 into the second output byte before publication; both synchronous MCS9 vendor captures retained this otherwise non-payload vector bit.</description>
              <bitOffset>14</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SPATIAL_REUSE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>15</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>15</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BANDWIDTH</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>19</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>3</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>GI_LTF</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>21</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>3</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>NSTS_AND_MIDAMBLE_PERIODICITY</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Complete dbg_dump_rx_ppdu shifts HE-SIG-A1 right by 23, masks three bits and prints the value as nsts_and_midamble_periodicity. The complete vendor private header uses the same name. A live 1T1R HE-SU RX vector 0x00e0591b with STBC set in HE-SIG-A2 produced encoding one: two space-time streams created from one spatial stream. This field is therefore not an unconditional NSS-minus-one value; with Doppler enabled it also carries midamble-periodicity information.</description>
              <bitOffset>23</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>3</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>7</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>VECTOR_REQUIRED_HIGH</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Complete formatter ORs 0xfc000000 before publication; both synchronous vendor captures retained all six bits.</description>
              <bitOffset>26</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>6</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>63</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x7C</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>HE_SU_SIGNAL_A2_LENGTH%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_hesig writes this second HE SU vector word at 0x201054f8-q*0x7c. It combines a bounded low control image with the complete HE APEP byte length shifted by eleven and a frame-class bit copied to bit 28. A-MPDU length 0x76 produced 0x1003b105; the live vendor throughput path independently reported length 0x061a in 0x1030d105. Complete libpp[pp_he.o]::ppCalSubFrameLength adds four to APEP when DMA metadata byte seven bit zero selects hardware HE-Control insertion, while leaving the low fourteen-bit MPDU length and DMA CCMP position unchanged. The vendor and open 24-byte raw S-MPDU paths both use APEP length 32, producing 0x00010105 with bit 28 clear.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x20</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>CONTROL_REQUIRED_0</name>
