        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x7C</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>DATA_LENGTH%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_len (size 0x128) writes the packed non-HE HT data length, MCS index and entry class here. Complete dbg_read_tx_sig names the fields as the HT40 length, MCS, EOF count and TXOP count. The exact vendor single-MPDU HT20 MCS0 callback image carried 0x0000006e for length 0x6e, proving entry class zero. The independent two-MPDU MCS7 capture carried 0x70400c2e for aggregate length 0x0c2e, proving entry class one for A-MPDU. The open direct-DMA A-MPDU HIL qualified the same entry class through complete BlockAck results. Legacy formatting does not consume this queue word.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x34</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>HT40_LENGTH</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>19</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
