        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x7C</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>LENGTH_CONTROL%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Canonical queue-vector length/rate/antenna image. Complete dbg_read_tx_sig names the low antenna-selection flags, RTS rate, HT20 EOF count and HT20 TXOP count. The upper four words of complete hal_attenna_init's eight-word traversal are these same queue-vector registers; its bit operations therefore use the canonical antenna fields below rather than a second BANK_CONTROL identity. Complete libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_len always publishes the mac_tx_get_rts_rate result in bits 13:6, including PPDUs without explicit RTS/CTS. The exact vendor single-MPDU HT20 MCS0 callback image carried 0x000002c4, proving entry class zero; the independent two-MPDU MCS7 capture carried 0x00400244, proving entry class one. Counterintuitively, the acknowledged HE20 DCM S-MPDU also requires entry class one and carries 0x004002c4. The open direct-DMA HIL qualified both the HT aggregate and HE S-MPDU images. Complete mac_tx_get_rts_rate maps legacy OFDM 48/24/54/36 Mbit/s to basic rate 24M, 12/18M to 12M, and 6/9M to 6M.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x38</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
