    <peripheral>
      <name>WIFI_MAC_TSF_TIMER</name>
      <description>Four-entry TSF timer bank recovered from all complete target, wakeup and enable/disable leaves. Each entry consists of one control word followed by its 32-bit target. The public index is guarded to zero through three by the target and timer-enable leaves; the dedicated wakeup leaves do not contain their own range check.</description>
      <baseAddress>0x2010D87C</baseAddress>
      <registers>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x8</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>CONTROL%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Per-timer control word at 0x2010d87c + index*8. Complete target accessors replace and return the low three bits, bits 34:32 of the 64-bit TSF target. Dedicated leaves set or clear wakeup bit 30, while the timer enable/disable leaves set or clear bit 31.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>TARGET_HIGH</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Bits 34:32 of the 64-bit TSF target. Complete libpp[hal_tsf.o]::hal_tsf_timer_set_target replaces them from its third argument and hal_tsf_timer_get_target returns them through its second output pointer; libpp[pm_twt.o]::pm_on_isr_twt_wake passes the high word of the stored 64-bit wake TSF there, and libpp[pm_twt.o]::pm_twt_set_target_tsf parks a timer with an all-ones low word and seven.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>3</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>WAKEUP_ENABLE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Set by hal_enable_tsf_timer_wakeup and cleared by hal_disable_tsf_timer_wakeup.</description>
              <bitOffset>30</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TIMER_ENABLE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Set by libpp[hal_tsf.o]::hal_enable_tsf_timer and cleared by hal_disable_tsf_timer.</description>
              <bitOffset>31</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>4</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x8</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-3</dimIndex>
          <name>TARGET%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Full 32-bit timer target written by libpp[hal_tsf.o]::hal_tsf_timer_set_target and returned through the first output pointer by hal_tsf_timer_get_target.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x4</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>VALUE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>32</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
      </registers>
    </peripheral>
    <peripheral>
      <name>COEX_HW_TIMER</name>
      <description>Six-entry coexistence timer bank. Complete libcoexist leaves address entry index as 0x2010f400 + index*0x10. The 48-event libcoexist[coexist_core.o]::coex_core_timer_idx_get table of the pinned archive returns timer indices zero through five or 0xff; index five is used only by the PHY grant-protect event 48.</description>
      <baseAddress>0x2010F400</baseAddress>
      <registers>
        <register>
          <dim>6</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x10</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-5</dimIndex>
          <name>CONFIGURATION%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Primary timer word. libcoexist[coexist_hw.o]::coex_hw_timer_set replaces both high nibbles and the low 24-bit tick image through separate fresh-read RMW operations. coex_hw_timer_force clears the low 24 bits; coex_hw_timer_unforce replaces them with 1000.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>PRIMARY_TICK_IMAGE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Low 24 bits returned by coex_hw_timer_tick_get for the first timer value. The exact counter epoch and units remain part of the reviewed timer conversion rather than the register geometry.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>24</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>16777215</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PARAMETER_2</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Low nibble of the third libcoexist[coexist_hw.o]::coex_hw_timer_set argument.</description>
              <bitOffset>24</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>15</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PARAMETER_1</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Low two bits of the second libcoexist[coexist_hw.o]::coex_hw_timer_set argument. Bits 31:30 are preserved by the complete vendor RMW.</description>
              <bitOffset>28</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>3</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_30_31_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Bits preserved by libcoexist[coexist_hw.o]::coex_hw_timer_set while PARAMETER_1 is replaced.</description>
              <bitOffset>30</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>6</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x10</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-5</dimIndex>
          <name>SECONDARY_TARGET%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. Secondary timer word. libcoexist[coexist_hw.o]::coex_hw_timer_set preserves the high byte and replaces the low 24 bits with the converted fourth timer-value argument.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x4</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>SECONDARY_TICK_IMAGE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>24</bitWidth>
              <writeConstraint>
                <range>
                  <minimum>0</minimum>
                  <maximum>16777215</maximum>
                </range>
              </writeConstraint>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_24_31_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established.</description>
              <bitOffset>24</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>8</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>6</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x10</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-5</dimIndex>
          <name>ENABLE_CONTROL%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. libcoexist[coexist_hw.o]::coex_hw_timer_enable sets bit zero here after clearing bit zero in the paired disable-control word. libcoexist[coexist_hw.o]::coex_hw_timer_disable performs the inverse transaction.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x8</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>ENABLE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_1_31_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established.</description>
              <bitOffset>1</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>31</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <dim>6</dim>
          <dimIncrement>0x10</dimIncrement>
          <dimIndex>0-5</dimIndex>
          <name>DISABLE_CONTROL%s</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. libcoexist[coexist_hw.o]::coex_hw_timer_disable sets bit zero here after clearing bit zero in the paired enable-control word. libcoexist[coexist_hw.o]::coex_hw_timer_enable performs the inverse transaction.</description>
          <addressOffset>0xC</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>DISABLE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_1_31_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established.</description>
              <bitOffset>1</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>31</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
      </registers>
    </peripheral>
    <peripheral>
      <name>COEX_EXTERNAL</name>
      <description>External coexistence control beside the coexistence timer bank. The complete hal_external_coexist.o leaves of the pinned libcoexist address these words at 0x2010f49c, 0x2010f4a0, 0x2010f4a4, 0x2010f4d0 and 0x2010f4d8 through fresh-read RMW operations; the GPIO matrix routing of the request, priority, grant and TX-line signals belongs to the platform, not to this block.</description>
      <baseAddress>0x2010F49C</baseAddress>
      <registers>
        <register>
          <name>PTI</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. External priority word. hal_set_extern_pti publishes three priorities in bits 11:0 in the basic modes, or a fixed advanced image in the follower mode; hal_clr_extern_pti clears them. hal_set_extern_coex_mode replaces bits 29:28 with the work mode, and hal_set_extern_pti_mode sets bits 31:30 in the one-wire leader mode and the advanced grant fields in the follower mode.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>PRIORITY_0</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Low nibble of the third hal_set_extern_pti argument in the basic modes; zero in the advanced mode.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PRIORITY_1</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Low nibble of the second hal_set_extern_pti argument in the basic modes; 0xf in the advanced mode.</description>
              <bitOffset>4</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>PRIORITY_2</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Low nibble of the first hal_set_extern_pti argument in the basic modes; zero in the advanced mode.</description>
              <bitOffset>8</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ADVANCED_PRIORITY</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. 0xf in the advanced mode with two or three wires, zero otherwise.</description>
              <bitOffset>12</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_16_19_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Advanced follower field: 1 with one wire, 0xc otherwise; hal_clr_extern_pti sets 0xf in the advanced mode.</description>
              <bitOffset>16</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_20_23_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Advanced follower field: 1 with one wire, 8 otherwise; hal_clr_extern_pti sets 0xf in the advanced mode.</description>
              <bitOffset>20</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_24_27_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Advanced follower field: 1; hal_clr_extern_pti sets 0xf in the advanced mode.</description>
              <bitOffset>24</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>WORK_MODE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Low two bits of the hal_set_extern_coex_mode argument: the external work mode (0 leader, 1 one-wire leader variant, 2 follower).</description>
              <bitOffset>28</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_30_31_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Set to 0b11 by hal_set_extern_pti_mode in mode 1 and in the follower mode; the leader mode leaves them unchanged.</description>
              <bitOffset>30</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>CONTROL</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. External control word written by hal_set_extern_coex_validity, hal_set_extern_coex_delay, hal_set_extern_coex_sync and the enable pair.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x4</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>VALIDATE_HIGH</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. hal_set_extern_coex_validity: set when the external grant is valid high.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>GRANT_DELAY</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. hal_set_extern_coex_delay replaces bits 8:1 with its argument; ic_set_extern_coex_params passes the grant delay in microseconds shifted left by four and masked to 0xf0.</description>
              <bitOffset>1</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>8</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ENABLE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. Set by hal_enable_extern_coex and cleared by hal_disable_extern_coex, after the other enable fields.</description>
              <bitOffset>9</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SYNC</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name. hal_set_extern_coex_sync replaces bits 19:10 with the low ten bits of its argument; hal_set_extern_pti_mode writes zero and then 0x14 in the leader mode.</description>
              <bitOffset>10</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>10</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_20_31_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Bits no external-coexistence leaf writes.</description>
              <bitOffset>20</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>12</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>ENABLE_1</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. hal_enable_extern_coex sets bit 14 and hal_disable_extern_coex clears it.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x8</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_0_13_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Bits no external-coexistence leaf writes.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>14</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ENABLE</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>14</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_15_31_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Bits no external-coexistence leaf writes.</description>
              <bitOffset>15</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>17</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>ENABLE_MASK_0</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. hal_enable_extern_coex sets bits 3:0 and hal_disable_extern_coex clears them.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x34</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>MASK</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_4_31_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Bits no external-coexistence leaf writes.</description>
              <bitOffset>4</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>28</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>ENABLE_MASK_1</name>
          <description>Project-assigned name. hal_enable_extern_coex sets bits 3:0 and hal_disable_extern_coex clears them. The same field is the IEEE 802.15.4 PTI offset that hal_set_IEEE802154_pti_offset replaces and hal_get_IEEE802154_pti_offset reads.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x3C</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>MASK</name>
              <description>Project-assigned name.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>BITS_4_31_OPAQUE</name>
              <description>Opaque: meaning not established. Bits no external-coexistence leaf writes.</description>
              <bitOffset>4</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>28</bitWidth>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
      </registers>
    </peripheral>
